# Grid B — U8 API surface (enum listing across a package)
#
# Gap target: enumerating PUBLIC enum types (not their values) is a
# meta-enumeration the current taxonomy has no SubjectKind for —
# SubjectTypeName is the closest but it does not distinguish
# string-typed enum aliases from regular type declarations.
#
# Ground truth (internal/types/analysis_ir.go + enums.go): public
# enum types in internal/types include Intent, Scenario, Complexity,
# AnswerShape, AnswerSubjectKind, TermKind, TaskNodeType, PipelineStage,
# AgentName, EdgeType, RequirementKind, PredicateAxis, etc. Positive
# anchor requires 4 of the most load-bearing to appear.
ID="u8b"
NAME="API surface — public enum types in internal/types"
QUESTION="列出 internal/types 包里所有公开（首字母大写）的字符串枚举类型名（例如 Intent 这类 'type X string' 加上 const 集合的）。"
# 2026-05-04 strictness audit: previous EC required `AnswerShape`
# but that type has been retired (shape-era cleanup, V2 block-only
# carrier migration; see types/answer_document.go comment). Replace
# with currently-extant enum type names verified via `grep -n
# 'type [A-Z][a-zA-Z]+ string' internal/types/`. Strict-bar: 4
# distinct extant enum types from the load-bearing set.
#
# 2026-05-30 false-positive repair: EXPECT_NOT_CONTAINS is space-
# tokenised and matched with `grep -iF` (case-insensitive substring).
# The "private" token collided with the LEGITIMATE enum value
# `private_only` of the (public) AnswerSymbolVisibility type — a
# correct, complete public-enum inventory FAILed on banned:private.
# The ban was mis-designed from the start: Go unexported types are
# lowercase (e.g. `tokenKind`) and never contain the literal substring
# "private", so this token never actually caught a private-type leak;
# it only fired on the word appearing inside a valid enum value or in
# scope prose ("private/lowercase types excluded"). Same lesson already
# encoded in read_combo_member_set_closure_scope.case. Drop "private";
# the "公开/首字母大写" scope is gated by the EXPECT_MATCHES_REGEX
# \b-anchored capitalised type names, and "lowercase" still weakly
# guards against listing unexported types.
EXPECT_CONTAINS="Intent Scenario Complexity QuestionFamily"
EXPECT_MATCHES_REGEX="\b(Intent|IntentExplain|IntentRootCause)\b
\b(Scenario|ScenarioGeneric|ScenarioConfigTrace)\b
\b(Complexity|ComplexitySimple|ComplexityComplex)\b"
EXPECT_NOT_CONTAINS="lowercase int.enum AnswerShape"
